  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With a binary string `s` **​​​​​without leading zeros**, output `true`​​​ *if* `s` *includes **no more than one contiguous segment of ones***. Otherwise, output `false`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"1001\"\nOutput: false\nExplanation: The string has two segments of size 1.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"110\"\nOutput: true\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= s.length <= 100`\n* `s[i]`​​​​ is either `'0'` or `'1'`.\n* `s[0]` is `'1'`.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"1001\"",
        "output": "false",
        "explanation": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"110\"",
        "output": "true",
        "explanation": ""
      }
    ],
    "notes": []
